%N A400357 Decimal expansion of (sqrt(33) - 3)/8.
%C A400357 Largest possible minimal pairwise distance of eight points inside an equilateral triangle with unit side length.
%C A400357 Equivalently, largest diameter of the circles in the densest packing of eight equal circles inside an equilateral triangle with side length equal to 1 + sqrt(3)*(this constant). If the circles had unit radius, the corresponding triangle would have side length A399814.
%H A400357 Paolo Xausa, <a href="/A400357/b400357.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%H A400357 Hans (J. B. M.) Melissen, <a href="https://doi.org/10.2307/2324212">Densest Packings of Congruent Circles in an Equilateral Triangle</a>, The American Mathematical Monthly, Vol. 100, Issue 10 (1993), pp. 916-925 (also available on <a href="https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324212">JSTOR</a>).
%H A400357 Wikipedia, <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Circle_packing_in_an_equilateral_triangle">Circle packing in an equilateral triangle</a>.
%H A400357 <a href="/index/Al#algebraic_02">Index entries for algebraic numbers, degree 2</a>.
%F A400357 Equals (A010488 - 3)/8.
%F A400357 Equals 2/(A399814 - 2*A002194).
%F A400357 Equals the largest root of 8*x^2 + 6*x - 3.
%e A400357 0.3430703308172535824813264335273661647775330572478...
%t A400357 First[RealDigits[(Sqrt[33] - 3)/8, 10, 100]]
%Y A400357 Analogous values for k points: 1 (k = 2, 3), A020760 (k = 4), A020761 (k = 5, 6), A152422 (k = 7), A010701 (k = 9, 10), A400358 (k = 11), A019913 (k = 12), A400359 (k = 13), A020773 (k = 14, 15).
%Y A400357 Cf. A399814.
%Y A400357 Cf. A002194, A010488.
%K A400357 nonn,cons,easy,new
%O A400357 0,1
